{"timestamp": 1779379175.043089, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 11, "data": {"caller": "player_2", "reason": "Charlie reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Eve"}, {"room": "electrical", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779379175.0438972, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 11, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379181.068733, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Alice's body in electrical when I arrived there this tick. Bob was already in the room with the body when I walked in, which is extremely suspicious. My route was navigation -> security -> electrical. I saw Alice earlier in navigation around tick 3-4, and tracked her moving through security toward electrical around tick 8. Bob being alone with her corpse in electrical when I arrived makes him my prime suspect. I'd also note Eve is dead somewhere too \u2014 so we've lost two Geese. Bob, explain yourself."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379217.3134131, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Charlie, are you kidding me?! That is a complete lie and a massive self-report! \n\nI was in electrical doing my calibration task\u2014Diana, you can vouch for me, you saw me there around ticks 7 and 8 working on it. Alice walked in from security at tick 10. Then Charlie, YOU walked in right behind her at tick 11, killed her right in front of me, and immediately hit the report button before I could even process what just happened! \n\nYou literally just admitted in your own statement that you were \"tracking her\" from Navigation through Security. You followed her and killed her! You just didn't expect me to still be in the back of electrical doing my task, so you panicked and self-reported to frame me. \n\nDiana, Frank, please see through this. Charlie tracked Alice, killed her, and self-reported. I'm voting Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379227.826829, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I can partially confirm Bob's story. I was in medbay at tick 3 when Bob came in from cafeteria, then I went to electrical myself and Bob was there at ticks 6, 7, and 8 \u2014 he appeared to be working on calibration. I left electrical for security after that, so I can't speak to what happened at ticks 10-11, but Bob's account of being in electrical doing his task lines up with what I witnessed.\n\nThat means Charlie's claim that Bob \"was already in the room with the body\" is technically true, but misleading \u2014 Bob had been there for at least 5 ticks doing a task. Charlie, by his own admission, followed Alice from navigation through security into electrical, arriving right when she died. That's a much more suspicious timeline.\n\nI'm leaning toward Charlie. Frank, what did you see?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379238.518373, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Honestly, I don't have much to contribute on the encounter front \u2014 my route was upper engine to oxygen, back to upper engine, then down to lower engine. I was on the west side of the map the entire round and didn't see anyone, so I can't vouch for or accuse anyone based on direct sight.\n\nBut based on what I've heard: Diana corroborates Bob being in electrical doing his task across multiple ticks (6, 7, 8). That's a strong alibi for Bob. Charlie, by his own admission, was actively tracking Alice and arrived in electrical at the exact tick she died, then immediately reported. \"Bob was already in the room with the body\" sounds damning until you realize Bob had been parked there doing a task the whole time \u2014 Charlie is the one who just arrived.\n\nThe timeline points to Charlie. I'm voting Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379256.641818, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Wait \u2014 I need to clarify something important. I was speaker 1, so I already spoke. But let me address what's been said because the narrative is being twisted against me.\n\nYes, I followed Alice's general path because I was doing my OWN tasks \u2014 navigation, then security, then electrical. That's a normal task route, not \"tracking\" her to murder her. I arrived in electrical at tick 11 and Alice was already dead on the floor with Bob standing right there. I reported immediately because that's what you're supposed to do.\n\nDiana, you say Bob was in electrical at ticks 6, 7, 8 doing calibration. Fine \u2014 but calibration is a quick task. If he finished it by tick 8, why was he still standing in electrical at tick 11 when Alice walked in? That's 3 ticks of just lingering in a room with no task left. That's the behavior of someone waiting to ambush.\n\nI'm a Goose. I did not kill Alice. Bob had means, opportunity, and was the only other person in the room. If you vote me out, you'll lose a Goose and the Duck walks free with majority closing in. Please think carefully before voting."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379264.034081, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379273.6161869, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Charlie, your rebuttal actually weakens your case. Calibration in electrical is a multi-step task with three panels \u2014 it's not unusual for it to take many ticks, and Bob may have been finishing it or doing a second visit. \"Lingering\" isn't evidence of murder when I directly witnessed him working on it across three consecutive ticks.\n\nMeanwhile, your own timeline is damning: you tracked Alice from navigation through security into electrical, arrived exactly at the tick she died, and reported instantly. You also framed your speech to make Bob look guilty by omitting that he'd been parked in electrical doing a task \u2014 something you would have seen the moment you walked in.\n\nBob has a partial alibi from me. You have opportunity, timing, and a misleading narrative. I'm voting Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379284.064075, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I'll keep this brief since I already laid out my reasoning earlier. Diana's testimony is the key here \u2014 she directly witnessed Bob doing calibration in electrical across ticks 6, 7, and 8. Calibration has multiple panels, so Bob still being there at tick 11 is completely consistent with finishing his task, not \"lingering to ambush.\"\n\nCharlie's rebuttal didn't help him. He admitted to following Alice's path, arrived at the exact tick of her death, and reported instantly \u2014 and his original speech conveniently omitted that Bob had been parked in electrical doing a task the whole time. That's a misleading framing from someone who claims to be a clean reporter.\n\nBob has corroboration from Diana. Charlie has opportunity, suspicious timing, and a narrative that doesn't hold up. I'm sticking with my vote: Charlie."}}
